 legacy financial world is starting to  understand is if you can understand the  communities if you can understand these  types of assets who the holders are you  gain an advantage by actually playing to  what they like just as we saw amc say  that they were going to do certain  things that their community really  wanted and just like when the amc ceo  was doing a live stream uh interview and  his computer fell and we saw that he was  sitting doing the interview in his  underwear and the internet went nuts  this is the same type of stuff you're  parlaying right into the hands of the  community which is ultimately what you  want because when you plug into that  network they'll do the work for you and  so already there are people who are  marketing the btfd ticker symbol and  they've got nothing to do with the  company they've got no ownership of it  literally no one can buy it yet but  still the bitcoiners are at work now  it's important to remember that these  are both futures bitcoin  etfs they are not spot  and so there are some challenges with it  it remains to be seen how closely will  they track the price it remains to be  seen what is the actual fee drag going  to be for rolling over the futures on a  monthly basis there's lots of questions  but it doesn't matter still 320 million  dollars of trading volume within the  first 30 minutes is highly impressive  but they're not the only etfs in the  game if we're going to have bitcoin  futures etf immediately people jump and  say well we're probably going to get  bitcoin spot etfs at some point too  and so barry silbert and michael  shunnenstein with grayscale they came  over the top and today they announced  that it is official they have filed the  necessary paperwork to convert the  world's largest bitcoin fund gbtc to  become the first american bitcoin spot  etf you got barry right here saying  grayscale and the new york stock  exchange formally kicked off the process  this morning to convert gbtc into the  first spot based bitcoin etf based in  the united states upon conversion they  will trade under the ticker symbol btc  now of course there are people that are  upset in the bitcoin community saying  using ticker symbol btc is confusing  because it confuses people that are  using btc on the internet not  necessarily to signal the stock but to  actually signal the asset itself again i  don't know what the right answer here is  but of course someone at some point was  going to lay claim to the btc ticker on  the publicly traded markets and so the  largest bitcoin fund in the world doing  it seems natural or seems obvious to me  but i also saw this tweet from michael  schunenstein the ceo of grayscale the  largest asset manager that is specific  to bitcoin and cryptocurrencies where he  said when i joined grayscale in 2014 we  sponsored one investment product the  grayscale bitcoin trust and we managed  about 60 million dollars in aum  today we have 15 products and we manage  more than 53 billion dollars in aun  absolutely nuts to see this type of  growth from an organization that was  started in 2013-2014  so we are likely only going to see this  continue whether it is the bitcoin  futures etfs where people are bringing  future based products into the  investment realm of asset managers and  asset allocators in the traditional  institutional world or whether it is  eventually that spot etf that will get  approved the conversion of gbdtc  and also many others who have made the  application  more and more investors of all types  individuals institutions financial  organizations and nation states are  going to continue to get access to these  assets but when you look at something  like bitcoin that has a fixed supply  there is likely to continue to be the  protection of purchasing power for years  and years to come because still there is  not that much adoption of these assets  there's only about 850 000 bitcoin  addresses that have one bitcoin or more  in them now again there are obviously  highly highly concentrated addresses as  well people who own way more than one  bitcoin but what we are likely to see is  that as more people come into the market  and as bitcoiners continue to solidify  in their minds that this is the greatest  store of value on earth whether you're  talking to a michael saylor or mark  cuban or somebody else they are going to  become more and more unwilling to sell  their bitcoin and so when you look at  this from a market structure standpoint  the etfs both futures based and spot  based along with things like interactive  brokers allowing for ras now to come  into the market there's a wall of demand  that is coming and bitcoiners are just  unwilling to sell the asset that they  believe is their reserve currency that  to me feels like the biggest story here  is that these etfs etc are going to  bring so much demand but it's not going  to matter people just aren't willing to  sell their bitcoin right now
 

